{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"188efb64588b7f06","type":"group","x":100,"y":-940,"width":740,"height":920,"label":"go to definition / jumping around"},
		{"id":"ff7b82aa2a762955","type":"group","x":-720,"y":-360,"width":800,"height":540,"label":"windows"},
		{"id":"39e65507c03e44c4","type":"group","x":-720,"y":-940,"width":780,"height":540,"label":"buffers / file search"},
		{
			"id":"9e9acc458e4f3e93",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"\n\n| Keys              | Action                                                      |\n| ----------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `<Tab>` `<S-Tab>` | Next, previous buffer                                       |\n| `<leader>x`       | Close the buffer                                            |\n| `<C-n>`           | Toggle the file tree (`a` new file, `r` rename, `d` delete) |\n| `<leader>ff`      | Telescope: find files (the Ctrl+P equivalent)               |\n| `<leader>fw`      | Telescope: live grep across the project                     |\n| `<leader>fb`      | Telescope: open buffers                                     |\n| `<leader>fo`      | Telescope: recent files                                     |\n| `<leader>ch`      | NvChad cheatsheet                                           |\nLive grep needs `ripgrep` installed, and `fd` makes file finding faster.\n\nTwo more Telescope pickers help with Godot-style navigation. Run them as commands:\n\n\n| Command                                    | Lists                                                |\n| ------------------------------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------- |\n| `:Telescope lsp_document_symbols`          | Functions, signals and variables in the current file |\n| `:Telescope lsp_dynamic_workspace_symbols` | Classes and functions across the project             |",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-680,
			"y":-900,
			"width":720,
			"height":480
		},
		{
			"id":"5e8d55a0c6cc5bbf",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"\n| Keys                                | Action                                                            |\n| ----------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `<C-w>v`                            | Vertical split                                                    |\n| `<C-w>s`                            | Horizontal split                                                  |\n| `<C-w>h` `<C-w>j` `<C-w>k` `<C-w>l` | Move focus left, down, up, right (NvChad also maps `<C-h/j/k/l>`) |\n| `<C-w>H` `<C-w>J` `<C-w>K` `<C-w>L` | Move the window to the far left, bottom, top, right               |\n| `<C-w>r`                            | Rotate windows                                                    |\n| `<C-w>x`                            | Swap with the next window                                         |\n| `<C-w>q`                            | Close the window                                                  |\n| `<C-w>o`                            | Close all other windows                                           |\n| `<C-w>=`                            | Equalize sizes                                                    |\n| `<C-w>+` `<C-w>-`                   | Taller, shorter                                                   |\n| `<C-w>>` `<C-w><`                   | Wider, narrower                                                   |\n| `<C-w>_`                            | Maximize height                                                   |\n| `<C-w>\\|`                           | Maximize width                                                    |\nCounts work, so `10<C-w>>` widens by 10 columns. Dragging split borders with the mouse also works. NvChad's `<leader>h` and `<leader>v` open horizontal and vertical terminals.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-700,
			"y":-320,
			"width":740,
			"height":480
		},
		{
			"id":"4c4e5c7bd9ca2c8e",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"\n| Keys             | Action                                                                   |\n| ---------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `gd`             | Go to definition (if unmapped, check `:verbose nmap gd`, or use `<C-]>`) |\n| `<C-o>`          | Jump back                                                                |\n| `<C-i>`          | Jump forward                                                             |\n| `<C-w>]`         | Open the definition in a new split                                       |\n| `K`              | Hover docs                                                               |\n| `grr`            | List references (Neovim 0.11 default)                                    |\n| `grn`            | Rename symbol (Neovim 0.11 default)                                      |\n| `gra`            | Code actions (Neovim 0.11 default)                                       |\n| `<C-LeftMouse>`  | Jump to the definition under the mouse                                   |\n| `<C-RightMouse>` | Jump back                                                                |\n| `<C-e>`          | scrolls view down one line at a time                                     |\n| `<C-y>`          | scrolls view up one line at a time                                       |\n| `<C-d>`          | scroll down half a page                                                  |\n| `<C-u>`          | scroll up half a page                                                    |\n| `<C-f>`          | scroll down a full page                                                  |\n| `<C-b>`          | scroll up a full page                                                    |\n| `<zz>`           | centers current line on screen                                           |\n| `<zt>`           | put current line at top of screen                                        |\n| `<zb>`           | put current line at bottom of screen                                     |\n",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":120,
			"y":-920,
			"width":680,
			"height":680
		}
	],
	"edges":[],
